# Develop-gate verification for pi-ensemble — AGENTS.md §1, mechanically.
#
# Without this file the resolver falls through to `npm run test`, which is three
# smoke tests out of ~120, no typecheck and no lint. The gate that is supposed
# to prove a developer's diff builds was proving almost nothing.
#
# The full §1 gate is `bun run build` too, but build writes into dist/ and this
# runs once per workstream worktree in parallel; the deeper suite lives in
# .pi/verify-cmd-full, which the ci step runs once.
#
# `--jobs-from-host` sizes the smoke pool from the host CPU count when
# PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TEST_JOBS is unset: 4 jobs on a host reporting 8+ CPUs, 2
# otherwise, an explicit ambient setting always winning. Measured on a 10-core
# host at the suite stage: 4 jobs → 4m49s, versus ~19 min under load at 2. That
# second figure is the reason this tier has its OWN bound (#1509): the suite
# tier is governed by PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_SUITE_TIMEOUT_MS (default 30 min, or
# .pi/verify-timeout-ms), NOT the 10-minute fast/smoke number it used to share.
# It is a flag rather than an inline `PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TEST_JOBS="${…:-$(getconf
# …)}"` prefix for a historical reason: until #1764 phase 2 the accept guard's A5
# arm admitted `bash …/verify-loop.sh` only when every following word was
# `--digest` or a test path, and an expansion-word was neither. The guard is now a
# path tripwire with no argv rules at all, so the flag spelling stays because it
# works, not because a guard requires it.
# See docs/configuration.md (`PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TEST_JOBS`).
#
# The typecheck names the compiler by PATH, not by alias (#1414/#1118). The
# `bun x` form is an npx-style lookup, and on the host this was filed from it
# resolved a GLOBAL TypeScript 7 that printed its usage and exited 0 — a
# typecheck gate that judged nothing while reporting every tree as typechecking.
# `node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc` is the CLI the `typescript`
# devDependency ships, so the compiler that answers is the one package.json
# pins, and no PATH entry can stand in for it. Same relative spelling as
# CHECKPOINT_TYPECHECK_CMD in
# extension/src/work-driver-cap-checkpoint-typecheck.ts, because both run with
# cwd = extension/. The gate that pins the two to one another is
# `test-verify-cmd-no-bare-alias` under extension/smoke-tests.
cd extension && node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json && node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.smoke-tests.json && cd .. && bun run check && cd extension && bash smoke-tests/lib/verify-loop.sh --jobs-from-host smoke-tests/test-*.ts
